Hi Robert,

Ahead of our storage review on Thursday, October 16 at 10:00, I=E2=80=99m sen=
ding the briefing and the separate group-summary workbook. As you requested i=
n July, the eligible counts are shown alongside the ratios: for 0, 24 and 48 =
h, the counts are 12, 11 and 11 and the group means are 100.0%, 99.1% and 82.=
0% of the 0 h mean, respectively. The 48 h group is 18.0% lower than the base=
line; the 24 h comparison is descriptive and does not establish equivalence.

The last slide is the question for the room: whether to adopt an inclusive 24=
 h maximum for routine work under the evaluated nonclinical supernatant measu=
rement workflow. It also sets out the proposed referral to Anthony for an und=
ocumented time or a known time over the limit. Could you make a decision on t=
he local operating limit at the meeting?

Thanks,
Melissa

